der **Settings > Webhooks**.\" Also \"Simply paste the URL and the events will be delivered\" implies all events are sent. Say whether readers choose which events to subscribe to.\n\n5. **No payload or request contract.** Missing: the HTTP method, the `Content-Type`, the JSON shape of each event, and the response the endpoint must return (for example, any 2xx within N seconds).\n\n6. **The event table may be incomplete.** \"The following events exist\" reads as a full list. If it isn't, say \"The following events are available\" or link to the full list.\n\n**Cleanup**\n\n7. **Cut the opening history.** The 2023 history, the \"two designs discussed\" detail, and \"polling was considered wasteful\" are background, not something a reader acts on. They will also go stale. Delete them.\n8. **Cut filler.** \"In this guide you will learn everything about webhooks\" makes a promise the page can't keep. Replace it with one sentence saying what the page covers and who it is for.\n9. **Remove \"Simply\"** and similar words (the Setup sentence above).\n10. **Heading wording.** \"Verifying signatures\" is fine, but \"Verify signatures\" in the imperative matches the steps you will add.\n\n**Before you publish**\n\nConfirm these with the implementation owner: the three event names, the `X-Signature` format, the HMAC input and key, the retry count and schedule, the disable and email behavior, and whether the secret can be retrieved again. I can rewrite the page once you have those values, or draft the verification section with placeholders for them now."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3118,"cache_read_input_tokens":19889,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3118},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_